!Sample_geo_accession = GSM7070762
!Sample_status = Public on Mar 01 2023
!Sample_submission_date = Feb 28 2023
!Sample_last_update_date = Mar 01 2023
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = NA
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: NA
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: HEK293T
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: Human embryonic kidney
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: wild-type
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: none
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = Sorting based on EGFP alone in HEK293T cells: cells were transduced with Pep30 lentivirus at low MOI, grown for 6 days, then FACS sort top and bottom 20% GFP cells. Sorting based on mCherry/EGFP ratio of WT and BAG6 KO cells: HEK293T as well as a clonal BAG6 knockout cell line were reverse transduced with the Pep30 library such that less than 30% of cells were transduced (thus are most likely a single integration per cell). The virus-containing media was removed after 24 hours and fresh media with 10% FBS and 1% PenStrep was added to the plates. After another 24 hours, transduced cells were purified based on their expression of mCherry. The transduced populations were returned to culture and allowed to grow out for an additional 6 days, with passaging as necessary to maintain confluence below 80%. After 6 days, both populations were sorted into 4 bins based on the ratio of EGFP/mCherry expression (High, mid-high, mid-low, and low) using a FACSAria cell sorter. The same mCherry/EGFP ratio gates were used for both WT and BAG6 KO cells. Sorted cells were spun down at 500 RCF for 5 minutes, washed once with 1000 uL PBS, spun down again, then frozen at -20 as a cell pellet.
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = HEK293T cells used in this study were purchased from ATCC, from which the BAG6 KO cells were derived using CRISPR/Cas9. Cells were cultured in DMEM with 4.5 g/L D-Glucose supplemented with 10% fetal bovine serum, 1% penicillin/streptomycin was added except when producing lentivirus. Low passage number cells were used and maintained under 90% visual confluency. Cells were maintained at 5% CO2 and 37 °C. HEK293T cells used in this study were confirmed to be negative for Mycoplasma Contamination and routinely tested using the MycoAlertTM Mycoplasma Detection Kit (Lonza, LT07-418).
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Genomic DNA was isolated from the cell populations using QIAGEN QIAamp DNA mini kit or Machery Nagel Nucleospin Tissue kit. For Pep13, genomic DNA from unsorted input cells was also extracted. In addition, RNA was also isolated using Trizol for Pep13 cells.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Genomic DNA was eluted in 50 uL of elution buffer. Libraries were then amplified using PCR with custom Illumina adapters, using Q5 high-fidelity PCR mix with 1000 ng input gDNA per sample. Libraries were amplified for a total of 24-27 cycles. After amplification, libraries were cleanup up using SPRISelect beads at a ratio of 0.7x. Purified library size was confirmed via gel and libraries were quantified using the KAPA qPCR Illumina library quantification kit. Libraries were subsequently pooled in a ratio based on the number of total cells collected from each sample. Pep13 RNA was reverse transcribed into cDNA and then preped using the same protocol described above.
!Sample_description = Pep13.txt
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were aligned to a custom index for the Pep30 library generated with the command bowtie-build in bowtie version 1.2.3 and the option -v 3 --best (best alignment with up to 3 mismatches). The counts of each Pep30 sequence were extracted from the alignment with the bash command cut -f 3 | sort | uniq -c.
!Sample_data_processing = Pep13: unique 40-nt read sequences were counted directly from fastq files. Sequences do not end with T were removed (encoded by the vector)
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: Custom
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Pep30lib-GFP-high-vs-low.txt: tab-delimited. Columns are: ID, DNA sequence, GFP_high read count, GFP_low read count, Peptide
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Pep30lib-GFP-mCherry-ratio.txt (both replicates): space-delimited. Columns are: ID Seq Peptide KO_high KO_midhigh KO_midlow KO_low WT_high WT_midhigh WT_midlow WT_low
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: Pep13.txt: tab-delimited. Columns are: DNA sequence, peptide sequence (stop codon decoded as *), peptide length, followed by read counts in libraries of DNA, RNA, GFP-high, and GFP-low
!Sample_data_processing = Library strategy: DNA amplicon sequencing
